From 6f67cd505e704d5df637cb1b4c94e298510320a3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GibaxLeGrand <48137851+GibaxLeGrand@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 11:00:36 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Runner: "Racers" is a row of Rule Settings, in the menu's own
 pictures
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Gibax (2026-11-26): "bouger le bouton default à côté de CONTINUE, pour
déplacer les options et pouvoir scroll dessus comme les autres"; "prendre
le même font que les options du menu et pareil pour le nombre"; "aligne
verticalement le choix du racers avec les autres options en colonne";
"enlève L et R vu que c'est une option gauche droite".

Rule Settings (the task 0x805A6660; its input 0x805A68C4) moves its cursor
over its entries (+31 of its data: six rows, Default, CONTINUE), changes a
row with left/right under entries - 2, writes the rows at CONTINUE (entries
- 1) and resets them at Default (entries - 2); the highlights follow the
same counts (0x805A74DC, 0x805A759C). While the Free Race menu (kind 0)
shows:
- nine entries: "Racers" at 6, Default 7, CONTINUE 8; four words keep the
  game's rows at six (0x805A699C, 0x805A6A00: left/right; 0x805A6A78:
  CONTINUE's loop; 0x805A6C30: Default's loop), put back when it closes;
- the runner changes the racers with left/right on entry 6 (D-pad or
  stick), Default sets them back to 8;
- Default's 2D object (the pool at [0x80682EF8], 192-byte objects, the
  element's function at +48, a 3x4 matrix at its head) moves by x -130,
  y +29: beside CONTINUE;
- the row is drawn with TSGME's pictures: the plate (texture 29), the word
  put together from the rules' words (texture 28: R, e, r of "Retire", a, s
  of "Laps", c of "Announce"), the digits in the values' column, the arrows
  (texture 30); selected or not as the game's rows (colours sampled).

Measured alone: the row reached with the cursor, 8 down to 5, CONTINUE
keeps the game's rules (laps, Announce, Level, Item, Air pit, Air Lost) and
the 5, a race of 5 racers; Default back to 8.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
